1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:05,422
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:12,303
[Tonio] <i>I'm going to talk.</i>

3
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:14,139
<i>I started working as Emilia's hit man</i>

4
00:00:14,222 --> 00:00:15,515
<i>when she was still a mayor.</i>

5
00:00:15,598 --> 00:00:17,767
<i>I have a list of the people</i>
<i>she had me kill.</i>

6
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:20,478
[Ivy] <i>It hurts, Diego, but I</i>
<i>have to stay away from you.</i>

7
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:23,898
<i>Especially now that my plans</i>
<i>are slowly unfolding.</i>

8
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:25,150
<i>The party hasn't released</i>

9
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:27,736
<i>an official list of candidates yet.</i>

10
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:30,780
<i>There's still so much that can happen.</i>

11
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:35,243
<i>I am Emilia Ardiente.</i>
<i>I'm destined to be a queen,</i>

12
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:37,537
<i>and my reign starts today.</i>

13
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,582
<i>-I'm backing out, Senator.</i>
<i>-You can't back out.</i>

14
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:44,252
<i>Because if you do that,</i>
<i>I will personally make sure</i>

15
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:48,465
<i>that this is going to be the end</i>
<i>of your political career.</i>

16
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:49,424
[Arnaldo] <i>It's about Mom.</i>

17
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:51,551
<i>The party won't be choosing her tonight.</i>

18
00:00:51,634 --> 00:00:54,054
<i>You can always choose another party.</i>

19
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:56,431
<i>But never your family.</i>

20
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:58,391
<i>I'm proud to present to you the person</i>

21
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:01,144
<i>who will complete the senatorial line up.</i>

22
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:04,022
<i>Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

23
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:07,942
<i>Governor Emilia will be taking</i>
<i>my grandfather's place.</i>

24
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:10,361
<i>That is the final decision of the party.</i>

25
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:11,362
<i>If that's the case,</i>

26
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:13,490
<i>then we will leave the political party.</i>

27
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:15,617
[Ivy] <i>Two birds, one stone.</i>

28
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,579
<i>Who's the better hunter now, Mr. Mayor?</i>

29
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:20,830
-[gunshot]
-[grunts]

30
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:23,958
[Jepoy] <i>Senator Alcantara was</i>
<i>ambushed. He's dead now.</i>

31
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:27,504
[Raul] <i>I won't lose you again,</i>
<i>no matter what.</i>

32
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:28,588
<i>You're mine.</i>

33
00:01:28,671 --> 00:01:30,173
[Ivy] <i>Jepoy, this feels different.</i>

34
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:32,884
<i>I want to make sure</i>
<i>if my mom really is dead.</i>

35
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:34,177
[Jepoy] <i>Is it because of your dream?</i>

36
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,095
[Ivy] <i>I want answers to everything.</i>

37
00:01:36,179 --> 00:01:37,722
<i>Because I want the Ardientes to pay</i>

38
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,599
<i>exactly what they owe me.</i>

39
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:41,351
<i>I want to see Tonio myself.</i>

40
00:01:41,434 --> 00:01:42,477
[Jepoy] <i>Are you ready to face</i>

41
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,937
<i>the person who killed your mother?</i>

42
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:49,526
[tense music playing]

43
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:02,789
How many people have you killed
for Emilia Ardiente?

44
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:04,791
Who are you?

45
00:02:04,874 --> 00:02:05,750
[gunshot]

46
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:08,002
[grunts, pants]

47
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:10,672
That's not important.

48
00:02:11,464 --> 00:02:14,092
Do you know everyone you killed?

49
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:17,804
-[gunshot]
-Ivy.

50
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,141
Do you know Camia Cruz?

51
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,685
Do you remember her?

52
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:29,399
The woman you raped and murdered?

53
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,359
Do you know her?

54
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:34,320
So what if I do?

55
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,573
-[gunshot]
-[grunts]

56
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:40,368
How did you kill Camia Cruz?

57
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:43,872
Answer me!

58
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:47,792
How did you kill Camia Cruz?!

59
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:55,300
<i>-Get out of here.</i>
<i>-Hey!</i>

60
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:58,970
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

61
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:01,723
You're the kid that got away.

62
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:03,600
You're still alive?

63
00:03:05,184 --> 00:03:07,812
Is that why you're interested in all this?

64
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,731
Do you want your children to suffer

65
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:11,232
the same fate that kid did?

66
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:14,444
I can do that.

67
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:16,821
[Ivy] I'll ask again.

68
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:19,032
How did you…

69
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:25,622
kill Camia Cruz?

70
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:31,127
Answer me! How did you kill Camia Cruz?!

71
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:32,462
How?!

72
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:39,010
I shot her in the leg.

73
00:03:39,802 --> 00:03:40,970
[grunts]

74
00:03:42,055 --> 00:03:42,972
<i>No!</i>

75
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:44,682
-[gunshot]
-[grunts]

76
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:47,602
[breathing heavily]

77
00:03:49,854 --> 00:03:52,273
But she was still breathing
when I buried her in the forest.

78
00:03:55,526 --> 00:03:58,613
[tense music playing]

79
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:05,203
Are you telling me my mother's alive?

80
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,126
It's possible she's still alive?

81
00:04:13,419 --> 00:04:14,295
Is that right?

82
00:04:19,884 --> 00:04:21,552
My mother is alive?

83
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:27,016
Is she still alive?

84
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,852
Answer me! Is my mother still alive?!

85
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:31,271
[Tonio] I don't know.

86
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:34,941
She'd have to be lucky
to get out of there alive.

87
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:36,526
You bastard!

88
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:39,696
You buried my mother alive?!

89
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:42,824
-You bastard! You monster!
-[gunshots]

90
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:45,034
[Tonio panting]

91
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:52,250
How could you do that to my mother?

92
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:03,594
You have kids, right?

93
00:05:05,763 --> 00:05:07,265
You have a family.

94
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:13,521
Do you want me to kill them, too?

95
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:21,529
I'm going to bury all of you alive.

96
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:26,993
I'll give you a taste
of your own twisted medicine.

97
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:32,040
No. Please have mercy on me.
Please have mercy.

98
00:05:32,123 --> 00:05:33,374
Forgive me.

99
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,210
I'm begging you. I have a
family! Forgive me.

100
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:37,503
Forgive you?

101
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:44,135
I don't know the meaning of that word.

102
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:50,433
Because what you did to me
and my family does not deserve

103
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:51,684
to be forgiven!

104
00:05:53,978 --> 00:05:55,563
-But…
-You bastard.

105
00:05:55,646 --> 00:05:56,564
[Tonio] But…

106
00:05:58,191 --> 00:06:01,402
But if your mother is still alive…

107
00:06:03,029 --> 00:06:07,033
it's possible that
the Ardientes might have her.

108
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:18,586
[tense music playing]

109
00:06:27,595 --> 00:06:30,973
Everyone who's connected to
my family is dying one by one.

110
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:34,852
First, Mr. Ramon,
and now, Senator Alcantara.

111
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:40,191
Uncle, what kind of curse
does the Ardiente name

112
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:41,776
have that requires people to die?

113
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:45,863
Diego, you can't blame all this
on your family.

114
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:48,324
No, Uncle.

115
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,910
Try connecting all those people.

116
00:06:51,661 --> 00:06:53,287
They all went against Mom.

117
00:06:58,126 --> 00:07:00,086
My conscience won't stop eating at me…

118
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:04,340
if I find out Mom
is connected to all this.

119
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:09,470
Diego, this house you bought is great.

120
00:07:10,888 --> 00:07:16,018
It's nice, huge, well-ventilated.

121
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:21,774
But, dear, why did you have
to get your own house?

122
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:23,860
You know you're always
welcome at our place.

123
00:07:26,779 --> 00:07:28,114
Oh, I know!

124
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,699
You're doing this…

125
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:32,660
because you're not getting
any younger, right?

126
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:36,205
It looks like you're getting ready…

127
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:39,167
because you're headed in that direction.

128
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,168
Oh…

129
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:42,503
You know what I'm talking about.

130
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:45,840
Well, how's it going? How's Miss Aguas?

131
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:49,802
With everything that's
happening right now…

132
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:52,513
I think it'd be selfish of me

133
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:54,849
if I prioritize my feelings for her.

134
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:59,228
Besides, just look at
what's happening around us.

135
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:03,357
The people here are dying one by one.

136
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:06,569
But…

137
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,782
I'll find time for it.

138
00:08:13,409 --> 00:08:14,702
I'll talk to her.

139
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:16,287
Good!

140
00:08:16,704 --> 00:08:17,872
[both chuckling]

141
00:08:17,955 --> 00:08:19,624
[Pandoy] Hey. Diego.

142
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:21,459
-Come on.
-Listen to me.

143
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:23,503
Um…

144
00:08:24,378 --> 00:08:30,176
You shouldn't give up on love
just because someone else did.

145
00:08:30,551 --> 00:08:32,887
Look at me and your Nanny Loring.

146
00:08:33,346 --> 00:08:34,555
Thump, thump, thump.

147
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:36,432
[giggling]

148
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:39,936
It's during times like this
that we need love the most.

149
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:40,895
That's true.

150
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:44,982
That's why you shouldn't deprive yourself

151
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:51,155
and your heart of your right
to love and be happy.

152
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,159
[both chuckling]

153
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:57,036
You guys are making me jealous.
Let's just go.

154
00:08:57,119 --> 00:08:58,704
We still have a lot of stuff to move.

155
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:02,792
-You're jealous, huh?
-You should be! Don't hesitate.

156
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:04,293
[grunts]

157
00:09:05,711 --> 00:09:07,922
[panting]

158
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:17,473
Jepoy.

159
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:26,440
There's a chance my mother's still alive.

160
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:32,446
[panting, sobbing]

161
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,784
My mother could still be alive.

162
00:09:44,709 --> 00:09:47,587
Why is she offering flowers to that girl?

163
00:09:48,546 --> 00:09:51,215
Maybe she thinks they're related,

164
00:09:51,299 --> 00:09:54,719
or maybe she thinks the girl
is her daughter!

165
00:09:57,263 --> 00:10:00,391
I think her memories are returning, Raul.

166
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:04,186
I have a feeling that my mother
is still alive.

167
00:10:04,478 --> 00:10:06,397
Let me just remind you that we dug up

168
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,149
your mother's remains. I personally--

169
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:11,193
I know. I know, Jepoy, I know!

170
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:12,612
But, there's a possibility

171
00:10:12,695 --> 00:10:14,447
that they weren't my mother's remains.

172
00:10:15,197 --> 00:10:17,116
Tonio said so himself.

173
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,619
He said he shot her in the leg…

174
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:21,203
and buried her alive.

175
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:24,165
What if that wasn't my mother's body?

176
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,960
That's next to impossible,
Auntie. I doubt it.

177
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:33,716
Love.

178
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:35,801
Love, stop that.

179
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:38,429
You have to rest. You're tired. Come on.

180
00:10:38,512 --> 00:10:39,972
You've been doing this for hours.

181
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:41,724
Let me just keep these for a while.

182
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:44,852
You can do this again later.
You're tired. That's enough.

183
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:59,200
[pensive music playing]

184
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:01,202
Love, that's enough.

185
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:03,329
You've been doing this for hours.

186
00:11:03,412 --> 00:11:05,206
You're tired. Just give this to me--

187
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:12,713
[Camia sobbing]

188
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:15,716
I told you to stop.

189
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:19,011
[wailing]

190
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,304
[Belen] Jasmin!

191
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,640
Raul, what's happening to her?

192
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:25,643
Stop it. Stop.

193
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:27,937
Jepoy, my heart's telling me…

194
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:31,690
that my mother's alive.

195
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:34,193
Jepoy…

196
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,780
I need to find my mother.

197
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:42,660
I won't stop until I find my mother.

198
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:46,122
[suspenseful music playing]

199
00:11:56,882 --> 00:11:58,008
[Belen] Jasmin.

200
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,263
[crying]

201
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:04,890
[instrumental theme music playing]

202
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:06,600
[Pandoy] <i>It's during times like this</i>

203
00:12:06,684 --> 00:12:08,185
<i>that we need love the most.</i>

204
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:11,147
<i>Don't deprive yourself</i>

205
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:17,319
<i>and your heart of your right</i>
<i>to love and be happy.</i>

206
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:24,702
[Tonio] <i>I shot her in the leg.</i>

207
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:27,788
<i>But she was still breathing</i>
<i>when I buried her in the forest.</i>

208
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:29,748
<i>If your mother is still alive,</i>

209
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:33,627
<i>it's possible that</i>
<i>the Ardientes might have her.</i>

210
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:51,020
[Arnaldo] <i>No target has ever</i>
<i>escaped my trap.</i>

211
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:56,525
<i>No matter what happens,</i>
<i>you will be mine, Ivy.</i>

212
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:02,531
[phone ringing]

213
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:10,873
[line ringing]

214
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:13,083
[phone ringing]

215
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:19,548
[line ringing]

216
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:28,807
[line ringing]

217
00:13:28,891 --> 00:13:31,018
[phone ringing]

218
00:13:36,106 --> 00:13:38,484
[line ringing]

219
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:46,367
[loud thud]

220
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:49,078
[murmuring]

221
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,710
-Diego.
-Yes, Nanny?

222
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:59,255
By the way, I forgot to show you this.

223
00:13:59,338 --> 00:14:02,758
Your copy of the land title
Miss Ivy gave you.

224
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:07,263
[soft music playing]

225
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,060
-Nanny.
-Yes?

226
00:14:14,436 --> 00:14:16,230
Do you think it's a bad thing…

227
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:20,943
that Ivy reminds me so much of Lily?

228
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:22,319
Hmm?

229
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:26,448
I just noticed they have
so many similarities.

230
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,160
How she pinches Butchoy's cheeks.

231
00:14:30,786 --> 00:14:31,996
How she likes pinwheels.

232
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:34,874
Her reaction when I took her
to Lily's old house

233
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:36,208
and the secret garden.

234
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:38,377
Now this.

235
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:40,129
What does this mean?

236
00:14:40,754 --> 00:14:42,131
Why is she helping us?

237
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:47,970
Well, because she's a good person.

238
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,847
I know, Nanny. I know Ivy's a good person.

239
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:52,391
But why is she always with Mom?

240
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:54,101
What does she need from my family?

241
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:55,895
Why is she in Poblacion Ardiente?

242
00:14:56,687 --> 00:15:01,483
Nanny, I have a hunch that Ivy
isn't just here for business.

243
00:15:05,362 --> 00:15:09,033
All right. Let's say that she is Lily.

244
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:11,702
Then why does she need to pretend?

245
00:15:14,121 --> 00:15:15,497
That's what I have to find out.

246
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:19,585
[soft music playing]

247
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:30,763
[exhales sharply]

248
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:37,895
[phone ringing]

249
00:15:41,231 --> 00:15:42,650
Hello, Vic. Let me talk to Grandpa.

250
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:43,692
<i>Yes, Mayor.</i>

251
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,529
[monitor beeping]

252
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:51,075
[sighs] <i>Grandpa, how are you?</i>

253
00:15:51,158 --> 00:15:52,826
<i>Aren't you awake yet?</i>

254
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:56,956
Well, just to give you an update.

255
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:01,001
Everything you've worked
so hard for is crumbling down.

256
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:02,586
Everything.

257
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:06,465
<i>And Mom, I don't understand her.</i>

258
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:09,677
<i>All her decisions are questionable.</i>

259
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:15,599
<i>She could be running us</i>
<i>into the ground, and…</i>

260
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:17,351
<i>I don't know. I don't know what to do.</i>

261
00:16:17,434 --> 00:16:18,394
<i>I need you.</i>

262
00:16:18,477 --> 00:16:22,398
[pensive music playing]

263
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:39,123
[suspenseful music playing]

264
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:53,220
[Natalie wailing]

265
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:58,726
Daddy!

266
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:03,772
Why did you leave me?

267
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:13,866
Daddy!

268
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:17,870
[sobbing]

269
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:31,091
I can't handle this.

270
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:34,678
I need to leave all of this.

271
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:36,472
I need to go.

272
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:39,600
What?

273
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:41,602
You're leaving? What about…

274
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:44,313
What about your family here?

275
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:48,942
Daddy's gone now.

276
00:17:52,196 --> 00:17:54,073
I don't have any family left.

277
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:58,202
Where will you go?

278
00:18:00,746 --> 00:18:01,955
I don't know.

279
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:05,209
Paris? I don't know.

280
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:13,300
[sniffles, sobs]

281
00:18:15,135 --> 00:18:16,345
Come here.

282
00:18:18,931 --> 00:18:20,390
I need to go.

283
00:18:22,434 --> 00:18:24,228
I need to forget.

284
00:18:24,311 --> 00:18:25,562
[wailing]

285
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:27,147
[shushes]

286
00:18:27,231 --> 00:18:29,441
I need to forget.

287
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:34,363
Help me.

288
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:38,534
Help me. Help me.

289
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:40,119
Yes. Yes. Yes.

290
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,538
I'm here.

291
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:46,792
Stop.

292
00:18:58,053 --> 00:19:00,639
Now that those wretched Alcantaras

293
00:19:00,722 --> 00:19:02,432
are out of our lives…

294
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:05,310
you can get closer to Ivy now.

295
00:19:08,021 --> 00:19:09,273
Arnaldo, son.

296
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:12,401
I know that you've been lusting after Ivy

297
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:14,570
the minute that you laid your eyes on her.

298
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:18,031
So, we need her now more than ever.

299
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:20,284
It's a win-win for you and me.

300
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:23,245
Does this mean
you're letting me pursue Ivy?

301
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:26,665
You said it yourself, right?

302
00:19:26,748 --> 00:19:29,209
That you're the charm of this family.

303
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:32,129
So, two birds with one stone.

304
00:19:33,213 --> 00:19:35,215
You know you need her.

305
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,301
And I need her, too.

306
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:40,053
That's why we need to have her.

307
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:50,814
Heart rate and pulse rate, all normal.

308
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:55,444
[suspenseful music playing]

309
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:58,030
Pupils are dilating normally.

310
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:02,784
Julio, can you hear me?

311
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:06,705
If you can hear me, please, nod.

312
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:10,959
[suspenseful sting]

313
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:26,225
Emilia, it's good you're here.

314
00:20:27,392 --> 00:20:28,727
Senator Jose is here to see you.

315
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:30,187
Oh, Senator!

316
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,564
Is there anything that I can do for you?

317
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:35,943
I'm here to warn you, Emilia.

318
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:38,237
The party won't stop

319
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:41,240
until we've caught
whoever had Pablo ambushed.

320
00:20:42,699 --> 00:20:43,909
[gasps]

321
00:20:43,992 --> 00:20:45,953
Senator, are you accusing me?

322
00:20:46,161 --> 00:20:47,621
Maybe I am, Emilia.

323
00:20:47,829 --> 00:20:49,748
I'm really offended, Senator.

324
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:53,001
You're threatening me in my own house.

325
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:55,087
I am not afraid of you, Emilia.

326
00:20:57,130 --> 00:21:00,634
What will Julio say
when he recovers and finds out

327
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:02,177
that you've cut ties with the party

328
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:04,680
and had his closest friend killed?

329
00:21:05,681 --> 00:21:07,599
You may leave now, Senator Jose.

330
00:21:13,021 --> 00:21:15,148
[dramatic music swelling]

331
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:17,276
I will make that senator pay.

332
00:21:17,859 --> 00:21:19,152
He'll see.

333
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:25,951
[phone ringing]

334
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,453
Hello, Dr. York.

335
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:30,289
Emilia. Good news.

336
00:21:31,873 --> 00:21:33,000
Good news?

337
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:35,043
Your dad. He's awake.

338
00:21:35,752 --> 00:21:36,837
What?

339
00:21:38,714 --> 00:21:40,090
[Dr. York] <i>You sound so surprised.</i>

340
00:21:42,926 --> 00:21:44,052
[exhales]

341
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:45,470
I am surprised.

342
00:21:46,263 --> 00:21:47,139
How is he?

343
00:21:47,222 --> 00:21:49,016
He's officially out of the coma.

344
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:52,311
And his test results are perfect.

345
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:55,188
He'll be home soon.

346
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,660
You'll be home soon, Julio.

347
00:22:14,291 --> 00:22:15,709
I'm getting impatient, Tonio.

348
00:22:16,418 --> 00:22:18,003
When are you going to give me the list

349
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:19,671
I've been asking you for?

350
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:22,591
I'll give you what you want.

351
00:22:23,216 --> 00:22:26,595
I'll help you, on one condition.

352
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:30,599
Make sure that my family is safe.

353
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:32,601
Are you serious?!

354
00:22:32,809 --> 00:22:35,187
You're demanding conditions?!

355
00:22:35,687 --> 00:22:37,397
Let me tell you something.

356
00:22:37,773 --> 00:22:41,318
You are in no position to demand anything!

357
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:44,362
Have mercy on me! I'm begging you!

358
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:45,489
[scoffs]

359
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:48,575
Why? Tell me.

360
00:22:48,909 --> 00:22:51,870
Did you show my mother mercy? Did you?

361
00:22:52,537 --> 00:22:54,289
I will never show you any mercy, Tonio.

362
00:22:54,372 --> 00:22:55,957
Not now, not ever.

363
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:01,004
Are you going to give me what I want,

364
00:23:01,088 --> 00:23:06,968
or do you want me
to have you killed right now?

365
00:23:08,386 --> 00:23:10,472
I will. I will.

366
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:11,765
What do you mean you will?

367
00:23:12,307 --> 00:23:13,683
Tell me!

368
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:15,769
I'll give you what you want.

369
00:23:16,603 --> 00:23:17,687
What?

370
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:19,731
I'll give you what you want.

371
00:23:20,023 --> 00:23:22,526
Louder. Say it.

372
00:23:23,443 --> 00:23:25,862
I'll give you what you want.

373
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:28,031
Very good.

374
00:23:29,407 --> 00:23:30,826
Now we're on the same page.

375
00:23:31,618 --> 00:23:33,078
You didn't have to give me a hard time.

376
00:23:33,161 --> 00:23:35,831
[tense music playing]

377
00:23:43,213 --> 00:23:44,214
Doc.

378
00:23:45,382 --> 00:23:48,510
Why did Jasmin throw a fit like that?

379
00:23:48,718 --> 00:23:51,638
That's actually the first time
that's ever happened.

380
00:23:51,721 --> 00:23:54,182
Does that mean her memories
are coming back?

381
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:55,183
Is that it?

382
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:58,562
That's possible.
But it's very rare in her case.

383
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:01,731
Especially since she suffered
catatonic depression.

384
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:03,483
And for 13 years,

385
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:06,486
she was neglected and wasn't
given any medical attention.

386
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:09,281
Doc, what are the things

387
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:13,660
that might trigger her memories
of the past to return?

388
00:24:13,785 --> 00:24:16,663
Well, it's possible that this is connected

389
00:24:16,746 --> 00:24:18,748
to what happened to her.

390
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:31,136
Doc, this all started when
she saw a picture of that woman.

391
00:24:32,262 --> 00:24:35,015
Who is this woman?
How is she connected to Jasmin?

392
00:24:36,892 --> 00:24:37,976
Uh…

393
00:24:38,059 --> 00:24:39,060
She's not, Doc.

394
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:41,646
What's confusing me now

395
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:44,858
is why she's so interested in this woman.

396
00:24:44,983 --> 00:24:47,485
Maybe this woman triggers
something from her past.

397
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:52,657
She probably looks like her mom,
sister, or best friend.

398
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:54,784
You know what, Raul?

399
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:57,495
Jasmin's case is very interesting.

400
00:24:57,871 --> 00:25:00,332
If this woman triggers a memory of her,

401
00:25:00,415 --> 00:25:02,167
you should expose her more often,

402
00:25:02,250 --> 00:25:05,128
alongside her electroconvulsive therapy,

403
00:25:05,212 --> 00:25:07,422
so she can get well faster.

404
00:25:08,298 --> 00:25:09,716
Maybe, not now.

405
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:12,594
I think she only needs a sedative.

406
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:14,888
That's what she needs to calm down.

407
00:25:15,597 --> 00:25:17,098
Why? Don't you want her to get better?

408
00:25:20,936 --> 00:25:21,686
It's not that.

409
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:25,565
I just think that some medicine
is enough to help her.

410
00:25:25,649 --> 00:25:28,526
Can you give her a prescription?

411
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:30,570
Don't worry. I'll give you an update.

412
00:25:32,572 --> 00:25:35,075
Uh, okay. If that's what you want.

413
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:36,326
Love. Let's go.

414
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:39,120
Come on.

415
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:44,167
Thank you, Doc.

416
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:45,168
Don't worry. I'll keep you posted.

417
00:25:45,252 --> 00:25:46,211
-All right.
-Thank you.

418
00:25:46,294 --> 00:25:47,337
Okay. Thank you.

419
00:25:55,804 --> 00:25:58,515
[tense music playing]

420
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:04,771
Thank you, Jepoy.

421
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:06,398
I already gave you what you want.

422
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:10,151
Please. I'm begging you. My family.

423
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:12,279
So what if you've given me what I want?

424
00:26:12,362 --> 00:26:14,322
Do you think I'll let you off
the hook just like that?

425
00:26:14,406 --> 00:26:16,032
Just for a book?

426
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:17,701
Jepoy.

427
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:21,288
Are you sure about this, Ivy?

428
00:26:26,751 --> 00:26:28,169
What are you gonna do to me?

429
00:26:29,296 --> 00:26:30,547
What are you going to do?

430
00:26:30,630 --> 00:26:33,383
Are you going to kill me
after I helped you?

431
00:26:35,719 --> 00:26:36,886
What would you like?

432
00:26:38,638 --> 00:26:40,807
You want me to thank you?!

433
00:26:41,224 --> 00:26:44,477
Should I be grateful just because of this?

434
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:48,064
Please, I beg you. Have mercy.

435
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:51,443
Believe it or not,
I already regret what I did.

436
00:26:52,485 --> 00:26:54,904
Please let me live. Please…

437
00:26:55,947 --> 00:26:57,782
I'll do everything you want.

438
00:26:59,242 --> 00:27:00,535
Have mercy.

439
00:27:02,579 --> 00:27:03,663
Stand up!

440
00:27:04,789 --> 00:27:06,291
I said stand up and sit!

441
00:27:09,794 --> 00:27:12,630
Right now, I don't feel sorry for you…

442
00:27:13,798 --> 00:27:16,384
because you deserve to die.

443
00:27:17,552 --> 00:27:19,846
I really want to kill you,

444
00:27:19,929 --> 00:27:25,435
but I don't want soil my hands
with your dirty blood.

445
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:27,270
So you should be thankful.

446
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:28,855
Have mercy on me.

447
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:30,482
Have mercy on my family.

448
00:27:31,483 --> 00:27:33,568
I regret what I did.

449
00:27:33,651 --> 00:27:34,986
Jepoy, you know what to do.

450
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:38,073
Don't kill me. Don't kill me.

451
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:41,368
Let me live. I'll do anything you want.

452
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:44,245
Jepoy, make sure you give him…

453
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:50,335
everything he wants before you kill him.

454
00:27:50,418 --> 00:27:53,713
No! Have mercy! Please!

455
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:56,508
Boss.

456
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,051
Boss, have mercy on me.

457
00:27:58,134 --> 00:28:00,804
-Back away.
-Boss, please, let me live.

458
00:28:00,887 --> 00:28:02,806
Think about my family.

459
00:28:02,972 --> 00:28:04,057
Dad?

460
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:06,726
Dad!

461
00:28:07,310 --> 00:28:08,686
-Sweetheart!
-Dad!

462
00:28:09,813 --> 00:28:11,022
Dad!

463
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:12,941
Dad!

464
00:28:21,991 --> 00:28:23,618
What will happen when Papa comes back?

465
00:28:24,327 --> 00:28:26,579
They're going to treat me
like trash again!

466
00:28:26,955 --> 00:28:28,957
All my plans will be for nothing.

467
00:28:29,833 --> 00:28:32,168
I'm going to be miserable again.

468
00:28:32,419 --> 00:28:36,339
Papa will have Raul killed.
This family is over!

469
00:28:37,006 --> 00:28:38,800
Calm down, Emilia.

470
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:41,970
You're stronger than this.
You can fix this.

471
00:28:43,388 --> 00:28:44,597
You're right, Auntie.

472
00:28:44,889 --> 00:28:47,016
Papa has no reason to return here.

473
00:28:48,184 --> 00:28:52,522
Or he shouldn't return at all.

474
00:28:54,649 --> 00:28:56,818
You deserve to be
where you are now, Emilia.

475
00:28:57,360 --> 00:28:59,279
You worked hard for all this.

476
00:29:00,238 --> 00:29:03,074
And I don't think Julio
has a place in this house…

477
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:05,660
or in this town…

478
00:29:07,954 --> 00:29:09,330
or in your life.

479
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:18,715
[Arnaldo] Mom!

480
00:29:19,048 --> 00:29:20,049
We need to talk.

481
00:29:21,176 --> 00:29:23,178
Why didn't you tell me
Grandpa's recovered?

482
00:29:23,970 --> 00:29:26,473
I spoke to his doctor.
He said he already told you.

483
00:29:26,556 --> 00:29:28,767
Arnaldo, I was about to tell you.

484
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:30,602
-But now that you know--
-Oh! Stop it.

485
00:29:30,685 --> 00:29:33,396
You're too obvious.
You aren't happy he's awake now.

486
00:29:33,688 --> 00:29:34,856
How dare you!

487
00:29:35,273 --> 00:29:37,776
Are you saying that I was happy
when Papa slipped into a coma?

488
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:41,321
I love him more than you know.

489
00:29:41,404 --> 00:29:42,530
You do?

490
00:29:42,864 --> 00:29:45,074
Then why did you never
visit him in America?

491
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,411
[clicks tongue, exhales]

492
00:29:48,953 --> 00:29:50,079
Don't worry.

493
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:51,498
I'll tell Grandpa you were so busy

494
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:53,082
taking over for him here.

495
00:29:53,792 --> 00:29:54,959
I'm going to bring him home.

496
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:03,885
[door slams shut]

497
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:15,772
Let's just wait for the results
of the DNA test after two days.

498
00:30:16,022 --> 00:30:17,106
Two days?

499
00:30:18,107 --> 00:30:19,818
Two days is too long.

500
00:30:20,276 --> 00:30:22,570
I need the results in 24 hours.

501
00:30:28,284 --> 00:30:31,621
Can you do it, Mr. Valenzuela?
Twenty-four hours?

502
00:30:33,665 --> 00:30:34,582
Yes, ma'am.

503
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:36,876
Thank you.

504
00:30:37,252 --> 00:30:38,795
Jepoy, please see him out.

505
00:30:47,595 --> 00:30:48,638
[exhales]

506
00:30:50,223 --> 00:30:54,227
Nanny, I can't wait any longer.
I need to know the truth.

507
00:30:54,561 --> 00:30:55,812
-Ivy…
-Emilia…

508
00:30:57,522 --> 00:30:59,816
If my mom is still alive,

509
00:30:59,899 --> 00:31:01,818
that doesn't mean
I'll let her off the hook.

510
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:05,280
Emilia will still rot in jail.
All of them.

511
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:07,991
All the Ardientes will rot in jail.

512
00:31:08,867 --> 00:31:09,993
I know, Ivy.

513
00:31:12,537 --> 00:31:13,705
[exhales]

514
00:31:19,210 --> 00:31:20,545
[Raul] Auntie, I don't like this.

515
00:31:20,962 --> 00:31:23,339
Her memories can't return.

516
00:31:24,799 --> 00:31:26,593
This might be better for her…

517
00:31:26,676 --> 00:31:28,303
to be Jasmin for the rest of her life.

518
00:31:30,138 --> 00:31:31,806
Don't you feel sorry for her, Raul?

519
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:33,850
She'd be more miserable

520
00:31:33,933 --> 00:31:36,352
if she remembers everything
that happened in her life.

521
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:40,189
[phone ringing]

522
00:31:43,151 --> 00:31:44,652
-Hello.
<i>-Raul.</i>

523
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:49,532
You need to come home now,
or I'll send my men after you.

524
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:51,159
All right. Fine.

525
00:32:10,428 --> 00:32:13,598
[soft music playing]

526
00:32:29,489 --> 00:32:33,076
<i>If I could take away</i>
<i>all the pain you feel…</i>

527
00:32:37,622 --> 00:32:39,540
<i>But how can I do that…</i>

528
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:42,377
<i>if you're hiding so many secrets from me?</i>

529
00:32:56,766 --> 00:32:59,352
[tense music playing]

530
00:33:03,439 --> 00:33:04,482
[grunting]

531
00:33:04,565 --> 00:33:07,485
-Hey! What do you want?!
-Ow!

532
00:33:08,194 --> 00:33:09,195
[grunting]

533
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:14,158
[tense music playing]

534
00:33:20,748 --> 00:33:21,833
Diego?

535
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:32,301
[grunting]

536
00:33:32,552 --> 00:33:35,304
Who ordered you to do this? Who?

537
00:33:35,763 --> 00:33:39,142
Senator Alcantara's daughter. Natalie.

538
00:33:40,685 --> 00:33:41,978
Dude, run!

539
00:33:42,061 --> 00:33:43,062
Hey!

540
00:33:43,563 --> 00:33:44,731
Diego!

541
00:33:48,192 --> 00:33:51,237
That stupid Natalie.
I don't have time for her.

542
00:33:52,321 --> 00:33:53,740
That witch.

543
00:33:59,412 --> 00:34:00,496
Are you sure you're okay?

544
00:34:01,122 --> 00:34:02,206
Did you break anything?

545
00:34:02,707 --> 00:34:05,251
[soft music playing]

546
00:34:08,546 --> 00:34:10,381
Ivy, I'm sorry. They got away.

547
00:34:12,300 --> 00:34:14,177
Diego, why are you apologizing?

548
00:34:15,636 --> 00:34:16,929
You don't have to.

549
00:34:17,597 --> 00:34:19,432
I should thank you.

550
00:34:19,807 --> 00:34:21,809
Thank you for coming to save me.

551
00:34:23,936 --> 00:34:25,104
But Natalie…

552
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:32,570
[sighs] I don't know why Natalie did that.

553
00:34:33,404 --> 00:34:36,574
But she'll get what she deserves
one of these days.

554
00:34:36,657 --> 00:34:39,911
Maybe not now, but soon enough.

555
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:43,039
But you have to be careful, Ivy.

556
00:34:43,247 --> 00:34:45,583
You should tighten your security.

557
00:34:47,293 --> 00:34:50,046
Diego, thank you.
But I can take care of myself.

558
00:34:52,548 --> 00:34:53,633
Uh…

559
00:34:54,884 --> 00:34:57,970
What made you come here?
Is there something you need?

560
00:35:00,848 --> 00:35:02,016
Uh…

561
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:07,313
I don't know, Ivy.

562
00:35:08,773 --> 00:35:11,025
I don't know why my feet led me here.

563
00:35:16,739 --> 00:35:18,116
I should get going now.

564
00:35:20,576 --> 00:35:21,619
Diego.

565
00:35:25,998 --> 00:35:27,291
Thanks again.

566
00:35:31,796 --> 00:35:32,797
Be careful.

567
00:35:44,392 --> 00:35:47,645
Did you hear me, Raul?
I said Papa is awake.

568
00:35:48,729 --> 00:35:49,856
I know.

569
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:52,024
Then why do you look so calm?

570
00:35:52,108 --> 00:35:53,067
In case you've forgotten,

571
00:35:53,151 --> 00:35:54,986
you're the one who strangled him.

572
00:35:55,319 --> 00:35:57,697
Emilia, I will never forget that day.

573
00:35:58,406 --> 00:36:00,283
Are you making fun of me, Raul?

574
00:36:00,700 --> 00:36:04,162
Once Papa orders your death,

575
00:36:04,787 --> 00:36:07,373
I don't know how
I can get you out of that.

576
00:36:07,623 --> 00:36:10,877
If there's someone who should
be worried, it's you, not me.

577
00:36:11,085 --> 00:36:13,462
After all the mistakes you've made…

578
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:16,174
I'm sure your father will go
after you first.

579
00:36:19,844 --> 00:36:24,140
But you have a solution for that, right?

580
00:36:25,266 --> 00:36:26,893
Just have him killed.

581
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:42,783
[suspenseful music playing]

582
00:36:54,170 --> 00:36:55,588
-Raul.
-What?

583
00:36:56,505 --> 00:36:57,798
Who is Jasmin?

584
00:37:01,135 --> 00:37:02,887
Jasmin? I don't know who that is.

585
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:06,057
You liar! Stop fooling me! What's this?!

586
00:37:06,140 --> 00:37:08,267
-Who's Jasmin?!
-Oh, come on!

587
00:37:09,143 --> 00:37:10,228
Who's Jasmin?

588
00:37:10,311 --> 00:37:11,729
What are you talking about? What Jasmin?

589
00:37:11,812 --> 00:37:12,855
So what's that?

590
00:37:15,566 --> 00:37:17,360
Do you know where I got this?

591
00:37:17,818 --> 00:37:21,197
I went to a gas station
and used their bathroom.

592
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:24,033
I used this to wipe myself.
Here, smell it.

593
00:37:24,116 --> 00:37:27,578
Stop it! Stop fooling me! Who's Jasmin?!

594
00:37:28,287 --> 00:37:30,539
If you won't tell me who your whore is,

595
00:37:30,623 --> 00:37:32,375
I'll find her myself!

596
00:37:32,458 --> 00:37:34,460
If you want, I'll even help you!

597
00:37:34,835 --> 00:37:36,796
Here.

598
00:37:36,879 --> 00:37:37,964
Problem solved.

599
00:37:38,047 --> 00:37:40,800
Why did you do that?! You bastard!

600
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:42,843
Stop it, Emilia.

601
00:37:43,010 --> 00:37:45,513
Instead of thinking about some name,

602
00:37:45,596 --> 00:37:47,848
you should worry about your father.

603
00:37:48,349 --> 00:37:52,186
Because he's going to take
everything you have right now.

604
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:56,816
[shower door slams shut]

605
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:59,360
[tense music playing]

606
00:38:05,408 --> 00:38:06,492
Ivy.

607
00:38:06,575 --> 00:38:08,869
Ivy, Mr. Valenzuela's here.

608
00:38:09,912 --> 00:38:11,998
He brought the DNA test results.

609
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:14,709
Miss Aguas.

610
00:38:17,044 --> 00:38:18,129
Thank you.

611
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:19,922
Please, show him out.

612
00:38:20,006 --> 00:38:21,924
-You're welcome.
-This way, sir.

613
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:27,638
[instrumental theme music playing]

614
00:38:50,244 --> 00:38:52,955
[dramatic music playing]

615
00:39:02,089 --> 00:39:03,341
[exhales]

616
00:39:09,430 --> 00:39:11,390
[gasping]

617
00:39:12,808 --> 00:39:14,018
There's a chance…

618
00:39:15,102 --> 00:39:16,812
There's a chance Mom's still alive.

619
00:39:17,772 --> 00:39:18,773
[exhales sharply]

620
00:39:20,941 --> 00:39:22,610
My mom could still be alive.

621
00:39:23,444 --> 00:39:24,487
Mom.

622
00:39:26,197 --> 00:39:27,239
Mom.

623
00:39:27,782 --> 00:39:28,783
Mom.

624
00:39:30,034 --> 00:39:31,327
My mom.

625
00:39:32,244 --> 00:39:34,372
You might still be alive.

626
00:39:35,122 --> 00:39:36,707
You might still be alive, Mom.

627
00:39:40,294 --> 00:39:43,005
Mom, I'll find you, wherever you are.

628
00:39:44,465 --> 00:39:47,426
I'm going to find you, Mom,
so we can be together.

629
00:39:48,761 --> 00:39:49,762
Mom…

630
00:39:52,181 --> 00:39:53,724
My mom is still alive.

631
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:57,269
Ivy. Ivy.

632
00:39:58,396 --> 00:40:02,733
[instrumental theme music
continues playing]

633
00:40:03,067 --> 00:40:04,944
There's a chance my mother's alive.

634
00:40:08,114 --> 00:40:11,242
There's a big chance
she's still out there.

635
00:40:12,952 --> 00:40:16,747
There's a huge chance my mother
is still alive, Nanny Carlotta.

636
00:40:22,795 --> 00:40:25,131
I want to see my mom.

637
00:40:26,048 --> 00:40:27,633
I need to find her.

638
00:40:29,176 --> 00:40:31,262
<i>I need to find my mother.</i>

639
00:40:32,555 --> 00:40:33,931
<i>I'm going to find her.</i>

640
00:40:36,559 --> 00:40:40,396
[dramatic music playing]

641
00:40:48,654 --> 00:40:50,406
<i>-Mom.</i>
<i>-Lily.</i>

642
00:40:50,489 --> 00:40:51,615
[gasps]

643
00:40:51,699 --> 00:40:53,159
[Camia cries]

644
00:40:54,493 --> 00:40:56,996
[groaning]

645
00:40:59,457 --> 00:41:01,750
[screaming]

646
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:12,928
Ivy? Ivy.

647
00:41:13,971 --> 00:41:15,306
-Jepoy.
-Why? What happened?

648
00:41:16,265 --> 00:41:17,516
Jepoy.

649
00:41:18,100 --> 00:41:19,810
Why? What's wrong?

650
00:41:20,728 --> 00:41:22,062
Jepoy, look.

651
00:41:23,564 --> 00:41:24,857
Negative.

652
00:41:25,483 --> 00:41:26,942
Jepoy, negative.

653
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:32,281
My hunch was right all along.
My dream was right.

654
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:36,869
I'm even more convinced
my mother is still alive.

655
00:41:39,538 --> 00:41:41,957
[breathing heavily]

656
00:41:50,549 --> 00:41:51,592
Lily?

657
00:41:54,887 --> 00:41:56,472
Lily? [gasps]

658
00:41:57,723 --> 00:41:58,849
Lily?

659
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:01,101
Lily? [gasps]

660
00:42:01,936 --> 00:42:03,020
Jepoy.

661
00:42:03,687 --> 00:42:06,857
Jepoy, please help me.
I need you even more now.

662
00:42:07,566 --> 00:42:10,402
Help me. We need to find my mom.

663
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:12,446
Jepoy.

664
00:42:13,072 --> 00:42:16,325
There's a huge chance
my mother is still alive.

665
00:42:21,747 --> 00:42:26,335
We'll do everything we can
to find your mother.

666
00:42:28,295 --> 00:42:29,964
[quietly] My mom is alive.

667
00:42:35,844 --> 00:42:37,888
I'm going to find her.

668
00:42:38,806 --> 00:42:40,140
My mom is alive.

669
00:42:50,109 --> 00:42:52,278
Mom, I'm going to find you.

670
00:42:53,779 --> 00:42:55,322
[crying] Lily.

671
00:42:56,657 --> 00:42:57,700
Lily.

672
00:42:57,783 --> 00:42:58,784
Jasmin?

673
00:43:00,494 --> 00:43:01,662
Who is Lily?

674
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:07,042
Who is Lily?

675
00:43:07,126 --> 00:43:10,879
[dramatic music playing]

676
00:43:21,724 --> 00:43:23,809
Let's start with the Ardientes.

677
00:43:24,518 --> 00:43:26,770
It's possible they're hiding my mother.

678
00:43:26,854 --> 00:43:29,565
I know that she's still here
Poblacion Ardiente.

679
00:43:29,690 --> 00:43:31,692
I'll keep an eye out for her.

680
00:43:31,775 --> 00:43:34,028
I'll even investigate
in the other towns if I have to.

681
00:43:34,653 --> 00:43:35,654
Good.

682
00:43:39,366 --> 00:43:42,995
[Ivy] <i>Where's my mom?</i>
<i>I told you to bring her to me.</i>

683
00:43:44,580 --> 00:43:46,248
[Valenzuela]
<i>Let's just wait for the results</i>

684
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:47,833
<i>of the DNA test after two days.</i>

685
00:43:48,042 --> 00:43:50,461
[Ivy] <i>I need the results in 24 hours.</i>

686
00:43:53,589 --> 00:43:56,425
Jepoy, where did you find those
remains we thought were hers?

687
00:43:56,675 --> 00:43:59,678
In the place where Tonio said
he buried your mom.

688
00:44:01,722 --> 00:44:03,265
Jepoy, someone took my mom.

689
00:44:03,932 --> 00:44:07,561
Someone took her,
replaced her with another body,

690
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:11,273
and put this ring on it,
just to fake her death.

691
00:44:11,357 --> 00:44:13,400
It's possible only one person
is behind all this.

692
00:44:13,859 --> 00:44:17,529
All this time, Jepoy,
all this time, my mom was alive!

693
00:44:19,406 --> 00:44:21,033
Jepoy, this is what you'll do.

694
00:44:21,116 --> 00:44:23,369
I want you to investigate that corpse.

695
00:44:23,452 --> 00:44:26,955
Find out who she was and who took her.

696
00:44:27,039 --> 00:44:30,542
Because I'm sure
that person has my mother.

697
00:44:39,426 --> 00:44:41,303
-Auntie?
-Hey, Raul.

698
00:44:44,515 --> 00:44:45,641
[Raul] How are you?

699
00:44:48,936 --> 00:44:50,896
It's good that she's feeling better now.

700
00:44:51,271 --> 00:44:53,732
How is she? Is she still
fiddling with those newspapers?

701
00:44:53,816 --> 00:44:57,444
Not anymore. She's quiet now.
But she was talking last night.

702
00:44:59,363 --> 00:45:00,989
What was she saying?

703
00:45:01,073 --> 00:45:02,699
[pensive music playing]

704
00:45:02,783 --> 00:45:03,784
Lily.

705
00:45:05,202 --> 00:45:06,203
Lily?

706
00:45:16,839 --> 00:45:18,298
Any updates, Jepoy?

707
00:45:18,382 --> 00:45:20,467
Ivy, I have the profile of all

708
00:45:20,551 --> 00:45:22,136
the missing persons here in the town.

709
00:45:22,219 --> 00:45:23,178
<i>This is from the police.</i>

710
00:45:23,637 --> 00:45:25,472
<i>I'm going to ask around to see</i>

711
00:45:25,556 --> 00:45:27,891
<i>which of these people have been</i>
<i>missing for a long time now.</i>

712
00:45:28,267 --> 00:45:30,310
One of them must have been used
as the decoy

713
00:45:30,394 --> 00:45:32,187
to replace your mom's remains.

714
00:45:32,771 --> 00:45:34,857
Thank you. Thank you, Jepoy.

715
00:45:34,940 --> 00:45:36,275
<i>I know this is an arduous process.</i>

716
00:45:36,358 --> 00:45:38,277
But we'll learn the truth eventually.

717
00:45:38,777 --> 00:45:41,655
I'm going to ask around, too.

718
00:45:42,156 --> 00:45:45,826
And I'll start with
the most powerful house here.

719
00:45:46,910 --> 00:45:48,162
<i>Emilia.</i>

720
00:45:48,954 --> 00:45:52,416
If she had my mom killed before…

721
00:45:52,791 --> 00:45:54,334
I have a hunch

722
00:45:54,626 --> 00:45:57,546
that my mom might be
in her custody if she survived.

723
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:00,466
What's your plan?

724
00:46:00,924 --> 00:46:01,884
It's simple.

725
00:46:02,968 --> 00:46:05,387
Just like what you did with that corpse…

726
00:46:06,930 --> 00:46:10,934
I'm going to dig up
all of Emilia's skeletons

727
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:12,895
and bring her fears to life.

728
00:46:14,646 --> 00:46:17,107
Ivy, can you repeat what you said?

729
00:46:17,191 --> 00:46:19,735
You're going to help me
with my image building?

730
00:46:20,068 --> 00:46:21,028
Yes.

731
00:46:21,111 --> 00:46:23,113
Grassroots campaign, Emilia.

732
00:46:23,238 --> 00:46:25,741
The Filipinos will slowly get to know

733
00:46:25,824 --> 00:46:30,287
and love Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

734
00:46:31,413 --> 00:46:32,372
Just tell me when.

735
00:46:32,456 --> 00:46:34,791
And I'm going to send
my team of experts over.

736
00:46:35,375 --> 00:46:37,461
Oh! Thank you, Ivy.

737
00:46:37,961 --> 00:46:39,505
That's one great news.

738
00:46:39,588 --> 00:46:41,590
And that's just what I need right now.

739
00:46:41,673 --> 00:46:44,760
Right after hearing the terrible news.

740
00:46:44,885 --> 00:46:46,637
What terrible news?

741
00:46:48,055 --> 00:46:50,557
Well, Papa's health is improving.

742
00:46:51,767 --> 00:46:52,935
He's coming back home.

743
00:46:53,018 --> 00:46:55,646
And that means my happy days are over.

744
00:47:00,359 --> 00:47:04,488
Then that means we need to
speed up your candidacy, Emilia.

745
00:47:04,947 --> 00:47:08,575
Why don't we release
a magazine article about you?

746
00:47:08,909 --> 00:47:10,744
The more controversial, the better.

747
00:47:12,871 --> 00:47:14,706
So, tell me, Emilia.

748
00:47:15,749 --> 00:47:20,754
What's the darkest past
of Emilia's administration?

749
00:47:27,553 --> 00:47:28,637
[exhales]

750
00:47:29,346 --> 00:47:32,849
Well, let's just say I've made
a lot of decisions in life

751
00:47:32,933 --> 00:47:35,561
that I didn't think through.

752
00:47:37,563 --> 00:47:39,898
That destroyed people's lives.

753
00:47:43,944 --> 00:47:45,028
Like what?

754
00:47:46,321 --> 00:47:50,325
Whose lives did you destroy, Emilia?

755
00:47:54,329 --> 00:47:55,747
Come on. You can tell me.

756
00:47:56,373 --> 00:47:58,792
You've already told me
so many secrets before.

757
00:47:59,626 --> 00:48:01,795
You can trust me. Promise.

758
00:48:07,801 --> 00:48:08,927
This family.

759
00:48:10,345 --> 00:48:12,848
All of them wiped out.

760
00:48:14,099 --> 00:48:15,809
But that was 13 years ago.

761
00:48:16,560 --> 00:48:21,148
It was too long ago that even
God may have forgotten about it.

762
00:48:21,648 --> 00:48:23,025
Don't you think, Ivy?

763
00:48:23,150 --> 00:48:26,570
[tense music playing]

764
00:48:32,200 --> 00:48:35,120
You had a whole family murdered?

765
00:48:36,079 --> 00:48:39,458
Not a single one survived?

766
00:48:40,751 --> 00:48:42,169
The whole family.

767
00:48:43,629 --> 00:48:45,672
Because when I tell my men
to do a good job…

768
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:48,759
it is indeed a good job.

769
00:48:52,054 --> 00:48:53,221
Hold on.

770
00:48:54,806 --> 00:48:57,851
Why are you so curious
about that family's story?

771
00:48:59,728 --> 00:49:01,647
Why all of a sudden, Ivy?

772
00:49:01,855 --> 00:49:05,734
[tense music playing]

773
00:49:22,417 --> 00:49:23,960
[Tonio] <i>I only killed the victims.</i>

774
00:49:24,044 --> 00:49:25,629
<i>But I'm not the one who buried them.</i>

775
00:49:25,712 --> 00:49:27,089
<i>-Who did?</i>
<i>-Mr. Noel.</i>

776
00:49:27,172 --> 00:49:28,924
<i>Who told you to do it?</i>

777
00:49:29,007 --> 00:49:30,842
<i>It was Raul. Raul Torillo.</i>

778
00:49:30,926 --> 00:49:35,555
<i>Who told you to take over</i>
<i>everything I left behind?</i>

779
00:49:35,806 --> 00:49:40,977
<i>You have no right sitting</i>
<i>in my goddamn chair!</i>

780
00:49:41,061 --> 00:49:42,562
<i>You're going to have Julio killed?</i>

781
00:49:42,646 --> 00:49:46,692
<i>Poblacion Ardiente is too small</i>
<i>for the both of us.</i>

